    <!-- Info page -->
    <string name="privacy_policy">Privacy Policy</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_content">WordMate Privacy Policy\n\nWordMate respects user privacy and is committed to protecting personal information while users use the application.\n\n1. Information We Collect\nWordMate may collect and store necessary information such as email address, display name, profile picture, learning progress, favorite word lists, study time, daily learning goals, and personal settings such as language, sound, dark mode, and reminder time.\n\n2. How We Use Information\nThis information is used to support login, synchronize learning data, save study progress, personalize the vocabulary learning experience, display learning statistics, and send daily vocabulary reminders if the user enables this feature.\n\n3. Data Synchronization\nWhen users log in, some learning data may be synchronized to Firebase so users can continue learning with the same account. WordMate does not sell, exchange, or share personal data with third parties for commercial purposes.\n\n4. Device Permissions\nThe application may request Internet permission for login, vocabulary lookup, and data synchronization. The application may also request notification permission to send study reminders. If users choose a profile picture from their device, the image is used only to display the personal profile inside WordMate.\n\n5. Data Protection\nWordMate tries to protect user data through secure authentication and storage services. However, users are responsible for keeping their accounts safe and should not share passwords or login information with others.\n\n6. User Rights\nUsers can update account information, change personal settings, turn off reminder notifications, log out, or request account deletion inside the application. When an account is deleted, some related learning data may not be recoverable.\n\n7. Policy Updates\nThis privacy policy may be updated when the application changes or adds new features. Continuing to use WordMate after the policy is updated means that users agree to the new content.</string>

    <string name="terms_of_service_content">WordMate Terms of Service\n\nBy using WordMate, users agree to follow the terms below.\n\n1. Purpose of Use\nWordMate is an application that supports English vocabulary learning through flashcards, review games, vocabulary lookup, favorite word lists, learning progress tracking, and daily study reminders. The application is designed for personal learning purposes.\n\n2. User Accounts\nUsers can register and log in using email or supported login methods such as Google and Facebook. Users are responsible for protecting their account information and should not share their account with others.\n\n3. Learning Data\nThe application may store learning progress, favorite word lists, game scores, learning goals, study time, and personal settings to help users track their learning process. When users log in, data may be synchronized to support use across multiple devices.\n\n4. User Responsibilities\nUsers must not use the application for cheating, damaging the system, accessing data without permission, affecting other user accounts, or using the application for improper purposes.\n\n5. Learning Content\nVocabulary content, examples, meanings, pronunciation, and learning suggestions in WordMate are provided for learning support. Users should combine the app with other learning materials, dictionaries, or teachers for better learning results.\n\n6. Third Party Services\nWordMate may use Firebase, Google Sign-In, Facebook Login, or vocabulary lookup APIs to provide login, synchronization, and lookup features. The use of these services may also be subject to the policies and terms of each provider.\n\n7. Service Changes or Interruptions\nWordMate may be updated, fixed, redesigned, or expanded with new features in the future. Some features may be temporarily interrupted due to maintenance, network issues, or third party service errors.\n\n8. Account Deletion\nUsers may delete their account if they no longer want to use the application. When an account is deleted, some related learning data may be removed and cannot be recovered.\n\n9. Limitation of Responsibility\nWordMate tries to provide a stable and useful learning experience, but it does not guarantee that the application will always be error free or perfectly suitable for every learning purpose.\n\n10. Acceptance of Terms\nBy continuing to use WordMate, users confirm that they have read, understood, and agreed to these terms of service.</string>
